	I really like the idea of monsters using items and weapons. It
would be much more 'realistic', and certainly more of a challenge!

	All these wonderful suggestions though, and nobody has caught
a major problem, that has been with the game since rogue; experience.
The main way to get it is by killing things. While this makes a little
sense for barbarians, knights, samurai, and valkyrie, it doesn't make
sense for wizards, clerics, healers, and rogues. It's the same thing
that made d&d such a joke. Shouldn't wizards get experience for
casting spells? How about clerics getting ep for turning undead,
blessing things, and sacrificing? healers for healing? rogues for
stealing?
	At the very least, why does a character still get ep for
killing a 'friendly' monster?

